HST PDF started on its own asks for a PDF file, and its launchers and shortcuts show HST PDF's icon.

- Linux pdf.desktop: Exec runs `--nodefault "service:org.hst.office.vi.PdfOpen?begin" %U
  service:org.hst.office.vi.PdfOpen`. The HST extension service notes the open windows at "begin";
  the files a file manager passes load in turn; the last argument then shows a file dialog limited to
  PDF files only when nothing was opened. Cancel leaves no Start Center (--nodefault) and no office
  without a window. Icon=pdf, and create_tree.sh installs the HST PDF icon set as <desktop id>-pdf.
- Windows: an "HST PDF" Start menu shortcut and, with "Create desktop shortcuts", a desktop shortcut
  (soffice --nodefault service:org.hst.office.vi.PdfOpen, AppUserModelID HASONTECH.HSTOffice.Pdf,
  tooltip "View PDF files and sign them digitally."). They belong to HST Draw's brand module: the
  Start menu one to program/pdf_app.ico (HST PDF's icon, copied into sysui/desktop/icons by the HST
  brand step and delivered by setup_native), the desktop one to desktophelper_pdf.txt with
  CREATEDESKTOPLINK=1, as the other app shortcuts.
- installer shortcut.pm: a non-advertised shortcut whose IconFile is an .ico of its own gets that
  icon (Icon table); the others keep showing their target's icon as before.
- The "HST Office" shortcut tooltip no longer describes LibreOffice and The Document Foundation:
  "HST Office, the office suite provided by HASON TECH. See https://hasontech.vn" (Vietnamese in
  l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_pdf_launchers_patch.py, tests/unit/test_pdf_open.py; windows-smoke shortcut check.
--- a/scp2/source/draw/folderitem_draw.scp
+++ b/scp2/source/draw/folderitem_draw.scp
@@ -37,4 +37,63 @@
     Key = "System.AppUserModel.ID";
     Value = "HASONTECH.HSTOffice.Draw";
 End
+
+// HST PDF: soffice asks for a PDF file (org.hst.office.vi.PdfOpen of the HST extension), the viewer opens
+// it. The shortcuts show HST PDF's own icon, shipped as program/pdf_app.ico; the Start menu shortcut
+// belongs to that file's component, so it comes and goes with HST Draw.
+File gid_Brand_File_Ico_Pdf
+    TXT_FILE_BODY;
+    Styles = (PACKED);
+    Dir = gid_Brand_Dir_Program;
+    Name = "pdf_app.ico";
+End
+
+File gid_Brand_File_Desktophelper_Pdf_Txt
+    TXT_FILE_BODY;
+    Styles = (PACKED);
+    Dir = gid_Brand_Dir_Program;
+    Name = "desktophelper_pdf.txt";
+    ComponentCondition = "CREATEDESKTOPLINK=1";
+End
+
+FolderItem gid_Folderitem_HstPdf
+    Name = "HST PDF";
+    ModuleID = gid_Module_Prg_Draw_Bin;
+    FolderID = gid_Folder_Staroffice51;
+    FileID = auto_brand_exe_soffice_exe;
+    IconFile = gid_Brand_File_Ico_Pdf;
+    IconID = 0;
+    ComponentIDFile = "gid_Brand_File_Ico_Pdf";
+    WkDir = gid_Brand_Dir_Program;
+    Parameter = "--nodefault service:org.hst.office.vi.PdfOpen";
+    Styles = (NON_ADVERTISED,USE_HELPER_FILENAME);
+    ALL_LANG(Tooltip, STR_FI_TOOLTIP_PDF);
+End
+
+FolderItem gid_Folderitem_HstPdf_Desktop
+    Name = "HST PDF";
+    ModuleID = gid_Module_Prg_Draw_Bin;
+    FolderID = PREDEFINED_DESKTOP;
+    FileID = auto_brand_exe_soffice_exe;
+    IconFile = gid_Brand_File_Ico_Pdf;
+    IconID = 0;
+    ComponentIDFile = "gid_Brand_File_Desktophelper_Pdf_Txt";
+    WkDir = gid_Brand_Dir_Program;
+    Parameter = "--nodefault service:org.hst.office.vi.PdfOpen";
+    Styles = (NON_ADVERTISED,USE_HELPER_FILENAME);
+    ALL_LANG(Tooltip, STR_FI_TOOLTIP_PDF);
+    ComponentCondition = "CREATEDESKTOPLINK=1";
+End
+
+FolderItemProperty gid_Fip_HstPdf_AppID
+    ShortcutID = gid_Folderitem_HstPdf;
+    Key = "System.AppUserModel.ID";
+    Value = "HASONTECH.HSTOffice.Pdf";
+End
+
+FolderItemProperty gid_Fip_HstPdf_Desktop_AppID
+    ShortcutID = gid_Folderitem_HstPdf_Desktop;
+    Key = "System.AppUserModel.ID";
+    Value = "HASONTECH.HSTOffice.Pdf";
+End
 #endif
